Answer: I think the approach you mentioned using dict() and a list of tuples is the way I would do it: [CODE] dict([(x, 3) for x in [_id, _if, _while, _lbrace, _println]] + [(_variable, 2)])
 [/CODE] If you really want to use a dict comprehension you can do something like this: [CODE] { x : 2 if x == _variable else 3
  for x in [_id, _if, _while, _lbrace, _println, _variable] }
 [/CODE]

