answer:
Most likely it's supposed to deal with three dimensional list of the following format: [CODE] people = [
    [['name', 'John'], ['age', 21]],
    [['name', 'Ann'],  ['age', 45]],
    [['name', 'Tom'],  ['age', 32]],
]

for person in people:
  # person is like [['name', 'Ann'],  ['age', 45]] here
  for (name, value) in person:
    # unpack [field_name, field_value] to name = field_name, value = field_value
    # so name is like 'name' (or 'age') and value is like 'Ann' (or 45)
    if name == 'name': print(value)
 [/CODE] Information for every person is stored in a list of pairs. Iterating over this [CODE] person [/CODE] list in that manner unpacks every pair into two separate variables: [CODE] name [/CODE] and [CODE] value [/CODE] that are later used to check field type and print value if it's name field. In the result this snippet will print names of all people.

