>> p = Person('Ozgur', '1234')
>> AttributeError: Denied.
 [/CODE]

Answer: The usual way is to use a "private" attribute starting with an underscore, and a read-only property for public access: [CODE] import operator

class Person(object):
    def __init__(self, name, ssn):
        self.name = name
        self._ssn = ssn
    ssn = property(operator.attrgetter("_ssn"))
 [/CODE] Note that this does not really hinder anybody to change the attribute [CODE] _ssn [/CODE] , but the leading [CODE] _ [/CODE] documents that the attribute is private.

