Answer: The psycopg2 dbapi driver buffers the whole query result before returning any rows. You'll need to use server side cursor to incrementally fetch results. For SQLAlchemy see server_side_cursors in the docs and if you're using the ORM the Query.yield_per() method . SQLAlchemy currently doesn't have an option to set that per single query, but there is a ticket with a patch for implementing that .

