The [CODE] collections.abc [/CODE] module defines the interfaces for things like [CODE] Mapping [/CODE] , [CODE] Sequence [/CODE] , and so on. By inheriting from the abstract base classes in that module, you get default implementations of some of the methods. So to be considered a [CODE] Mapping [/CODE] , your class definition should look something like this: [CODE] class MyMapping(collections.abc.Mapping):
