Answer: Letâs say weâre evaluating [CODE] quick_power(1234, 2) [/CODE] . The evaluation goes like this: [CODE] quick_power(1234, 2) [/CODE] [CODE] quick_power(quick_power(1234, 1), 2) [/CODE] [CODE] quick_power(1234 * quick_power(1234, 0), 2) [/CODE] [CODE] quick_power(1234 * 1, 2) [/CODE] [CODE] quick_power(1234, 2) [/CODE] â¦as you can see, it eventually starts evaluating back where we started, so you end up with infinite recursion. Without giving you the solution, I advise you to think: if we have a constant exponent (here, 2), is there a way you can compute that without having to do it recursively?

