Understanding django admin readonly_fields I created some code to differentiate between two usergroups in Django admin, resulting in showing all fields readonly or only some of them, which are set directly in the ModelAdmin class. At first here is the code: [CODE] class PersonAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):
    readonly_fields = ('created_at','created_by',)

def get_form(self, request, obj=None, **kwargs):
    if obj:     # we are in edit mode
        if request.user.is_superuser:
            self.readonly_fields = ()
