The ModelAdmin is only instantiated once for all requests that it receives. So when you define the readonly fields like that, you're setting it across the board permanently. As long as you're running Django 1.2+, there's a [CODE] get_readonly_fields [/CODE] method you can use instead for exactly this purpose: [CODE] class MyModelAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):
