answer:
[CODE] for [/CODE] loops in Python always go forward. If you want to be able to move backwards, you must use a different mechanism, such as [CODE] while [/CODE] : [CODE] i = 0
while i < 5:
    print(i)
    if condition:
        i=i-1
    i += 1
