Answer: Here's a class decorator to make a class a multiton: [CODE] def multiton(cls):
   instances = {}
   def getinstance(id):
      if id not in instances:
         instances[id] = cls(id)
      return instances[id]  
   return getinstance
 [/CODE] (This is a slight variant of the singleton decorator from PEP 318.) Then, to make your class a multiton, use the decorator: [CODE] @multiton
class MyObject( object ):
   def __init__( self, arg):
      self.id = arg
      # other expensive stuff
