How do I remove entries within a Counter object with a loop without invoking a RuntimeError? [CODE] from collections import *
ignore = ['the','a','if','in','it','of','or']
ArtofWarCounter = Counter(ArtofWarLIST)
for word in ArtofWarCounter:
    if word in ignore:
        del ArtofWarCounter[word]
 [/CODE] ArtofWarCounter is a Counter object containing all the words from the Art of War. I'm trying to have words in [CODE] ignore [/CODE] deleted from the ArtofWarCounter. Traceback: [CODE]   File "<pyshell#10>", line 1, in <module>
    for word in ArtofWarCounter:
RuntimeError: dictionary changed size during iteration
 [/CODE]

answer:
Don't loop over all words of a dict to find a entry, dicts are much better at lookups. You loop over the [CODE] ignore [/CODE] list and remove the entries that exist: [CODE] ignore = ['the','a','if','in','it','of','or']
for word in ignore:
    if word in ArtofWarCounter:
        del ArtofWarCounter[word]
 [/CODE]

