How do I get the maximum value? You don't need to "get" it. The root is exactly the maximum, that's a defined property of a heap. If you feel tough to understand heap sort, this chapter will be extremely helpful. I rewrote your code: [CODE] def swap(i, j):                    
    sqc[i], sqc[j] = sqc[j], sqc[i] 

def heapify(end,i):   
    l=2 * i + 1  
    r=2 * (i + 1)   
    max=i   
    if l < end and sqc[i] < sqc[l]:   
        max = l   
    if r < end and sqc[max] < sqc[r]:   
        max = r   
    if max != i:   
        swap(i, max)   
        heapify(end, max)   

def heap_sort():     
    end = len(sqc)   
    start = end // 2 - 1 # use // instead of /
    for i in range(start, -1, -1):   
        heapify(end, i)   
    for i in range(end-1, 0, -1):   
