 [/CODE] However - if you know what the types should be, then that's much better than brute forcing like this... And you could utilise the [CODE] ast [/CODE] library to do some of the work, which will be potentially more flexible, require less hits on the try/except mechanism (and reads a bit easier, but does require a little bit of work on pre-processing the inputs) [CODE] def guess2(text):
    from ast import literal_eval
    tokens = (t.strip() for t in text.split(','))
    for token in tokens:
        try:
            token_value = literal_eval(token)
            token_type = type(token_value)
            yield token_value, token_type
        except ValueError as e:
            yield token, type(token)
 [/CODE]

