You need to rewrite this rather heavily. First, use [CODE] quote_ident [/CODE] and [CODE] quote_literal [/CODE] instead of manual quoting. Better, use [CODE] format() [/CODE] with the [CODE] %I [/CODE] and [CODE] %L [/CODE] specifiers for identifiers and literals if you're on a newer PostgreSQL version. Also, try to avoid building strings iteratively like that. Build with an expression with [CODE] CASE [/CODE] s where possible There's no need for any [CODE] varchar(300) [/CODE] business. Just use [CODE] text [/CODE] . Your [CODE] ELSE [/CODE] clauses seem to contain the same thing as your [CODE] IF ... THEN [/CODE] . I've removed them. Try using [CODE] RETURN QUERY EXECUTE [/CODE] or, if you're getting just one value, [CODE] EXECUTE ... INTO [/CODE] . [CODE] DECLARE
