answer:
Your objects must be hashable (i.e. must have [CODE] __eq__() [/CODE] and [CODE] __hash__() [/CODE] defined) for sets to work properly with them: [CODE] class Test(object):
    def __init__(self):
        self.i = random.randint(1, 10)

    def __eq__(self, other):
        return self.i == other.i

    def __hash__(self):
        return self.i
