Signal handling in Pylons I have a pylons project where I need to update some in-memory structures periodically. This should be done on-demand. I decided to come up with a signal handler for this. User sends [CODE] SIGUSR1 [/CODE] to the main pylons thread and it is handled by the project. This works except after handling the signal, the server crashes with following exception: [CODE] File "/usr/lib/python2.6/SocketServer.py", line 264, in handle_request
