Answer: You can do something like this with coroutines: [CODE] def stoppable_iter(iterable):
    it = iter(iterable)
    for v in it:
        x = yield v
        if x:
            yield
            return
 [/CODE] And then use it like this: [CODE] it = stoppable_iter(range(10))
for i in it:
    for j in range(10):
        print i, j
        if i*j == 20:
            it.send(StopIteration) # or any value that evaluates as True
            break
 [/CODE] And a brief example of how it works: [CODE] >>> t = stoppable_iter(range(10))
>>> t.next()
0
>>> t.next()
1
>>> t.send(StopIteration)
>>> t.next()
Traceback (most recent call last):
  File "<stdin>", line 1, in <module>
StopIteration
 [/CODE]

