As pointed out by Veedrac in his answer , this problem has already been solved in Python 3.3+ in the form of the [CODE] ChainMap [/CODE] class: [CODE] function_that_uses_dict(ChainMap({1001 : "1001"}, big_dict))
 [/CODE] If you don't have Python 3.3 you should use a backport, and if for some reason you don't want to, then below you can see how to implement it by yourself :) You can create a wrapper, similarly to this: [CODE] class DictAdditionalValueWrapper:
    def __init__(self, baseDict, specialKey, specialValue):
        self.baseDict = baseDict
        self.specialKey = specialKey
        self.specialValue = specialValue

