There's nothing built-in that I know of that behaves as you want it.  Strictly speaking, this isn't a real subset as it should be doing set comparisons as it is in Python (where every item in a set is unique) but it should be simple to cook one up. [CODE] public static bool IsSubsetOf<TSource>(this IEnumerable<TSource> lhs, IEnumerable<TSource> rhs)
{
    // O(m+n)
    var contents = rhs.ToList();
    foreach (var item in lhs)
    {
        if (!contents.Remove(item))
            return false;
    }
    return true;
}
