>>> z = dict(x.items() + y.items())
>>> z
{'a': 1, 'c': 11, 'b': 10}
 [/CODE] If you use Python 3, it is only a little more complicated.  To create [CODE] z [/CODE] : [CODE] >>> z = dict(list(x.items()) + list(y.items()))
>>> z
{'a': 1, 'c': 11, 'b': 10}
 [/CODE]

