Answer: In C++ adding elements to a vector may cause reallocation of the contained data, which will invalidate all iterators. That means you can't loop over the vector using iterators (which is what the range-based for loop does) while also inserting new elements. You can however iterate using indexes and use the vector size as condition, since indexes will always be the same.

